{"name":"Falafel","hex":"#aa7711","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"falafel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Middle Eastern food in the form of balls made from chickpeas or broad beans and other ingredients, often served in a pita.","A pita with falafel balls as a filling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/falafel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Falafel","blocks":[{"text":"Falafel is a deep-fried ball or patty-shaped fritter of Egyptian origin that features in Middle Eastern cuisine, particularly Levantine cuisines. It is made from ground fava beans, chickpeas, or both, and mixed with herbs and spices before frying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Falafels_2.jpg/330px-Falafels_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falafel"},{"title":"Falafel (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Falafel is a 2006 Lebanese film written and directed by Michel Kammoun. It world premiered on September 16, 2006, at the Ayam Beirut Festival. Falafel is Kammoun's first feature film, and was produced by Elle Kensington."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/97/Falafelthemovie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falafel_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/PACK_DONKEYS_PARKING_NEAR_A_%22FALAFEL%22_VENDOR_IN_THE_OLD_CITY_OF_JERUSALEM._%D7%97%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%9D_%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%9E%D7%93%D7%99%D7%9D_%D7%9C%D7%99%D7%93_%D7%93%D7%95%D7%9B%D7%9F_%D7%A4%D7%9C%D7%90%D7%A4%D7%9C_%D7%91%D7%A2%D7%99%D7%A8_%D7%94%D7%A2%D7%AA%D7%99%D7%A7%D7%94_%D7%91%D7%99%D7%A8%D7%95%D7%A9%D7%9C%D7%99%D7%9D..jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/PACK_DONKEYS_PARKING_NEAR_A_%22FALAFEL%22_VENDOR_IN_THE_O